      "section_id": "trainingwebopsaiml_06_detail_section",
      "section_order": 6,
      "html_id": null,
      "element": "section",
      "section_name": "Detail Section",
      "section_heading": "Good questions.",
      "heading_level": "h2",
      "eyebrow": "A little more clarity",
      "subheading": "",
      "description": "",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "The Cloud Bootcamp teaches cloud platforms and DevOps from the ground up. WebOps & AI/ML assumes your team already runs production systems and adds two things: sharper reliability practice and applied AI on top of it. Cloud-first teams often run the Bootcamp first.",
        "Against a staging or sandboxed mirror of it, yes, under NDA if required, which is where the monitoring and incident-response exercises get real. We don't run break-and-fix drills on live production, for obvious reasons.",
        "Something small and genuinely yours: for example a log-triage assistant or an alert summarizer wired into your stack during the sessions. The point is your team shipping one real AI-assisted improvement, not a slide about possibilities."
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A little more clarity"
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Good questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "How does this differ from the Cloud Computing Bootcamp?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The Cloud Bootcamp teaches cloud platforms and DevOps from the ground up. WebOps & AI/ML assumes your team already runs production systems and adds two things: sharper reliability practice and applied AI on top of it. Cloud-first teams often run the Bootcamp first."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Can the training run against our actual infrastructure?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Against a staging or sandboxed mirror of it, yes, under NDA if required, which is where the monitoring and incident-response exercises get real. We don't run break-and-fix drills on live production, for obvious reasons."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "What does \"a working AI-assisted tool\" actually mean?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Something small and genuinely yours: for example a log-triage assistant or an alert summarizer wired into your stack during the sessions. The point is your team shipping one real AI-assisted improvement, not a slide about possibilities."
        }
      ],
